extends layout

block headContent
	title About

block content
	h1.h3 About
	hr

	p This tool is a simple, self-hosted explorer for the BLAKE2b chain of Bitcoin Knots, driven by RPC calls to your own node. It is easy to run but lacks some features compared to database-backed explorers.

	p Blocks up to the hard fork are shared with Bitcoin. From the fork on, blocks use BLAKE2b proof of work and the extended header, and difficulty is reported as the expected number of hashes per block. The node details page shows the fork height.

	p Whatever reasons one might have for running a full node (trustlessness, technical curiosity, supporting the network, etc) it's helpful to appreciate the "fullness" of your own node. With this explorer, you can not only explore the blockchain (in the traditional sense of the term "explorer"), but also explore the functional capabilities of your own node.

	p This is a fork of 
		a(href="https://github.com/janoside/btc-rpc-explorer") BTC RPC Explorer
		|  by Dan Janosik and its contributors, released under the MIT license. The design, the pages and most of the features are theirs.

	p This fork adds support for the BLAKE2b chain of Bitcoin Knots, the red theme, security hardening (CSRF protection, a limit on failed logins, TLS verification for Electrum servers), and a rewrite of the code in TypeScript with tests and a Docker image. See the 
		a(href="https://github.com/2rdzy/btc-rpc-explorer#credits") credits
		|  for details.

	p Pull requests are welcome! 
		a(href="https://github.com/2rdzy/btc-rpc-explorer") github.com/2rdzy/btc-rpc-explorer
